## 🧘 Critical Thinking Questions (Ask yourself while coding)

1. *Since I used `JOINED` strategy, every time I fetch a generic `Device`, Hibernate does a JOIN on all 3 tables (Device, Camera, Thermostat) to figure out what type it is. Is this slow? Would `SINGLE_TABLE` be faster? Why didn't we use `SINGLE_TABLE`?*
2. *I made `NetworkIdentity` Lazy. But when I convert Entity -> DTO in the Service layer, I accidentally called `device.getNetworkIdentity().getIp()`. Did I just trigger the query I was trying to avoid? How do I handle DTO conversion without accidentally triggering Lazy loading?*

**Do you accept this challenge?** 🛡️ This project is technically "smaller" than a full app, but much **deeper** in complexity.
